1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,381
An earthquake lasts seconds.

2
00:00:02,381 --> 00:00:05,238
The cost stays with you.

3
00:00:05,238 --> 00:00:10,476
Imagine a small shop in Colombia: a cracked window, lost

4
00:00:10,476 --> 00:00:13,333
stock, a day without income.

5
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:20,000
The loss can sit below a deductible—and still be more than
your savings.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,172
I built Aivy Quorum around parametric cover: agree on an

7
00:00:24,172 --> 00:00:27,966
earthquake trigger and a fixed payout before it happens.

8
00:00:27,966 --> 00:00:31,000
Verify the event, not every broken window.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,949
Let's try Medellín.

10
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:38,308
Choose the place, review the premium, and see the
conditions.

11
00:00:38,308 --> 00:00:43,667
The history chart compares premiums for the same eight-
hundred-dollar payout.

12
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:47,077
It's a model, not a forecast.

13
00:00:47,077 --> 00:00:49,1000
Damage alone doesn't trigger payment.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,174
Now I pay with funded test tokens.

15
00:00:54,174 --> 00:00:56,261
No wallet extension.

16
00:00:56,261 --> 00:01:02,000
This creates a real cover NFT, publishes the terms, and

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,130
schedules the payout on Hedera.

18
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:07,217
Here's the receipt.

19
00:01:07,217 --> 00:01:14,000
The demo tokens have no cash value, but these transactions
really happened.

20
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,628
The agent pays three oracle services through Blocky402 using
x402.

21
00:01:19,628 --> 00:01:23,209
Each checks the policy's recorded conditions.

22
00:01:23,209 --> 00:01:26,279
Here are the payment receipts.

23
00:01:26,279 --> 00:01:32,419
These checks found no matching earthquake, so the payout
stays locked.

24
00:01:32,419 --> 00:01:35,1000
Buying data is not buying approval.

25
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,059
This is why Hedera matters.

26
00:01:39,059 --> 00:01:43,647
The agent signs the exact transfer in advance.

27
00:01:43,647 --> 00:01:48,235
Two of three oracle keys must also sign.

28
00:01:48,235 --> 00:01:53,333
Then Hedera executes it, without a separate executor
transaction.

29
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:57,412
This recorded mainnet experiment moved four HBAR.

30
00:01:57,412 --> 00:02:02,000
Those were controlled signatures—not a real earthquake
claim.

31
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,217
The workflow is deterministic, with spending limits and
saved transaction IDs.

32
00:02:07,217 --> 00:02:12,000
Even all three oracle keys cannot spend without the agent.

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,418
Here, I'm moving demo-account tokens, not the locked cover
reserve.

34
00:02:17,418 --> 00:02:23,328
Our Hedera Agent Kit Axelar plugin builds the bridge to
Sepolia.

35
00:02:23,328 --> 00:02:26,776
Uniswap's Trading API prepares the swap.

36
00:02:26,776 --> 00:02:30,224
Review, confirm, and inspect both receipts.

37
00:02:30,224 --> 00:02:36,134
A Hedera-native app reaches EVM liquidity without its own
Solidity contracts.

38
00:02:36,134 --> 00:02:41,552
Test tokens and gas are supplied, so a judge can

39
00:02:41,552 --> 00:02:45,000
try it without a wallet extension.

40
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,379
Uniswap also provides a real position NFT, fee collection,
and withdrawal.

41
00:02:50,379 --> 00:02:52,172
That's trading liquidity.

42
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:58,000
Funding earthquake cover is different: deposits go into one
shared Hedera pool.

43
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,467
Here, twenty-five test tokens buy twenty-five ARPS.

44
00:03:01,467 --> 00:03:04,500
Earnings and exits aren't enabled yet.

45
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,667
Brokers earn referral commissions.

46
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:11,000
A future business could charge insurance partners service
fees.

47
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,133
From Aivy, I can also set a monthly cover budget.

48
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:18,933
The first policy is real.

49
00:03:18,933 --> 00:03:25,000
Future purchases follow saved limits, and I can pause the
agent anytime.

50
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,200
I can ask Quorum what is happening.

51
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:32,600
It explains policies and networks, links real receipts, and
has

52
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,000
no authority to move funds.

53
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:41,194
Earlier Aivy infrastructure and the Uniswap and Axelar
plugins already existed.

54
00:03:41,194 --> 00:03:46,871
Quorum connects guarded policies, paid verification, native
settlement, cross-chain access,

55
00:03:46,871 --> 00:03:51,000
bounded monthly purchasing and a read-only companion.

56
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,889
The goal is simple: less uncertainty when people need help.

57
00:03:55,889 --> 00:03:59,000
A promise you can actually verify.
